      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:25:3",
      "text": [
        " رَأَيْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا سَجَدَ يُحَرِّكُ ثَلَاثَ أَصَابِعَ مِنْ أَصَابِعِهِ وَاحِدَةً بَعْدَ وَاحِدَةٍ تَحْرِيكاً خَفِيفاً كَأَنَّهُ يَعُدُّ التَّسْبِيحَ ثُمَّ رَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Abdullah Bin Aamir, from Ali Bin Mahziyar, from Muhammad Bin Ismail who said, ",
          "‘I saw Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> when he<sup>asws</sup> performed <span class=\"iTxt\">Sajdah</span>, moved three fingers from his<sup>asws</sup> fingers, one after the other, with a slight movement as if he<sup>asws</sup> was counting the Glorifications, then raised his<sup>asws</sup> head’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amir from Ali ibn Mahziyar from Muhammad ibn Isma’il who has said the following: “I saw abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, when prostrating, move three of his fingers one after the other slightly as if counting rosary and then raise his head from prostration.” "
        ]
      }
